It was embellished on all sides) with various animals, diverse trees and big mansions made by Viśvakarmāt himself. It was adorned all around with artificial forests and all the trees there bore flowers and fruits, spreading their branches like to umbrellas and having golden and silvern pavements under them. 'The son of Brahma and artist of gods.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-14-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5012035","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ffac437c37ea4273e29b348bafbf9d461bd404470cbc14cdb47b44e670107668","compact":"c4c281c804a99ff95b0d80e883fe173db59ce6c99146f555fbf420108311130c","nasal":"c4c281c804a99ff95b0d80e883fe173db59ce6c99146f555fbf420108311130c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-12-36","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":12,"verse":36,"english":"And that great monkey beheld there one golden Singsapa* tree surrounded on all sides with golden pavements. 'A tree (Dalbergia Sisu).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-14-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5012036","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79c6c86f11fd346d4425f6c69a88bb1693140e79e7c2c828b3e094aac36b568b","compact":"42113523035501823baa274aa82672112491683d8ea8f78cd22cfec11a0afb8b","nasal":"ee801f0c6096d4abad08cb0730ce94c696ba1e141eeefa861ea606fbb0abc1e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-12-37","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":12,"verse":37,"english":"And he saw the glebe, the hill streams and many a golden trees resembling the fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-14-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5012037","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f43a06dd574348389c70fa